      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 4,
          "section": "2. Experimental procedure",
          "quote": "The seven designed alloys (Table 1) were used to evaluate the validity and applicability of the present model. These alloys were fabricated using argon gas atomization, powder sieving (-270 mesh), and hot isostatic pressing at sub-solvus temperatures and 103 MPa for 4 h. The heat treatment procedure entailed sub-solvus solution annealing for 1 h, salt quenching or air cooling, and two-step aging heat treatments at 870 °C for 1 h, air cooling, 650 °C for 24 h, then air cooling.",
          "table": "Table 1",
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "4c4febe98fdb2038:part:001"
