      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "15",
          "section": "4. Calculation of mechanical properties",
          "quote": "In the seven new alloys considered in the present work (Table 1), the average grain size was 4 ~ 5 µm (Fig. 8). Analyses using TEM, EPMA, and EDS detected Cr-rich M23C6 carbides, Ti-rich MC carbides, borides, and primary γ′ precipitates (1 ~ 2 µm) at the grain boundaries of individual alloys, but did not detect topologically close-packed (TCP) phases such as σ and µ. Inside the grains, secondary (300 ~ 500 nm) and tertiary (40 ~ 100 nm) γ′ precipitates were commonly observed, but η phases based on the Ni3Ti crystal structure were observed only in Alloys 1 and 3.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
